{"term":"intermediate","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:78f1620fb910f83558","definition":"Being between two extremes, or in the middle of a range.","example":"Then, being on his knees between my thighs, he drew up his ſhirt, and bared all his hairy thighs, and ſtiff ſtaring truncheon, red-topt, and rooted into a thicket of curls, which cover’d his belly to his navel, and gave it the air of a fleſh-bruſh: and ſoon I felt it joining cloſe to mine, when he had drove the nail up to the head, and left no partition but the intermediate hair on both ſides.","pos":"adj","synonyms":["average","intermediate","middle","middling","mild","medium","medial","moderate"],"antonyms":["extreme","intense"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/intermediate#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:86b1b617a1c2d42415","definition":"Anything in an intermediate position.","example":"In Oklahoma, an intermediate license holder may not carry more than one non-family member in the vehicle unless accompanied in the front seat by a licensed driver over 21 years of age.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/intermediate#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:0e58284a4100d64fb8","definition":"An intermediary.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/intermediate#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:e4f35464f2a33a13ce","definition":"An automobile that is larger than a compact but smaller than a full-sized car.","example